---
import { LINKS } from '../lib/site';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Why does Codex say "API-equivalent"?',
    a: 'Codex is often used on a flat ChatGPT plan. The figure is what the tokens would cost through the OpenAI API, not necessarily what you paid.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How accurate are the numbers?',
    a: 'Estimates at the built-in rates. Repeats are collapsed, unpriced models are flagged, and runtime skips gaps over 30 minutes.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What happens when the agents delete old transcripts?',
    a: 'Nothing is lost: a daily archive keeps every day it has seen.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Windows won’t run it. Why?',
    a: `The build is unsigned. Smart App Control <b>On</b> blocks it, a build from source too. <a href="${LINKS.smartAppControl}">How to turn it off</a>.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Where does it keep its data?',
    a: `In <code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\\AI Usage Native</code>, or the folder <code>AIUSAGE_DATA_DIR</code> names. <a href="${LINKS.config}">What is in it</a>.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Is it free?',
    a: `Yes, under the <a href="${LINKS.license}">MIT license</a>. Bugs and questions go to the <a href="${LINKS.issues}">issue tracker</a>.`,
  },
];
---

<section class="section" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
      <h2 id="faq-title">Questions, answered.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="list">
      {
        faqs.map((item) => (
          <details>
            <summary>{item.q}</summary>
            <p class="muted" set:html={item.a} />
          </details>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .list {
    max-width: 52rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 18px 2px;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
  }

  summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  summary::after {
    content: '+';
    flex: none;
    color: var(--accent-bright);
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  details[open] summary::after {
    content: '−';
  }

  details p {
    padding: 0 2px 20px;
  }
</style>
